!MesaLibs - riscos-mesa's shared libraries
==========================================

Programs built as "mixed" programs with the riscos-mesa devkit (UnixLib
linked into the program, the other libraries shared) load OpenGL (OSMesa),
EGL, GLU, GLUT, SDL 2 and OpenAL from here, through !SharedLibs. Programs
that use them share one copy of each library in memory.

Install: copy !MesaLibs into !Boot.Resources (open !Boot, then Resources).
Programs that need it boot it when they start. It sets MesaLibs$Path and
runs DAClamp, which lifts RISC OS 5's 128 MB limit on dynamic areas given a
maximum size (OS_DynamicArea 8,0,-1,0, as !GTKLibs does). !SharedLibs puts
every shared library in one such area, sized when the first program loads
one, so the limit has to go before then: keep !MesaLibs in !Boot.Resources.

Also needed:
- !SharedLibs with ld-riscos/so/2 (GCCSDK 8 or later; Iris includes one),
  also in !Boot.Resources;
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, and ARMEABISupport.

The libraries (in lib):
  libOSMesa/so/8    OpenGL 2.1 and OpenGL ES 1.1/2.0 (Mesa 20.3.5)
  libEGL/so/1       EGL for RISC OS
  libGLU/so/1       GLU 9.0.1
  libglut/so/3      freeglut 3.8.0
  libSDL2-2.0/so/0  SDL 2.32.10
  libopenal/so/1    OpenAL Soft 1.19.1

Programs that link the devkit's static libraries (as before) don't need
this. https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-mesa - licences in LICENCES.txt
there: Mesa (MIT), GLU (SGI B 2.0), freeglut (MIT/X), SDL (zlib), OpenAL
Soft (LGPL 2 or later: being a shared library, it can be replaced).
